<title>CANADA: Sale of CN Rail, Petro-Can give Ottawa C$2 billion.</title>
<headline>Sale of CN Rail, Petro-Can give Ottawa C$2 billion.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal government said on Tuesday it will receive about C$2.0 billion in 1996-97 for the sale of its shares in Petro-Canada and the sale of the Canadian National Railway Co.</p>
<p>The money represents the final instalments from the 1995 sale of the railway and all but 20 percent of the shares of Petro-Canada, the government said in its announcement of the 1997 budget.</p>
<p>The $2.0 billion has already been accounted for in deficit calculations for previous years and will not affect the 1996-97 budget. However, the money allows the government to reduce its borrowing requirements for that amount in 1996-97.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
